is</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Wild</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mathews</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Schachter</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kroll</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferguson</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Lancee</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Seven-year follow-up of speech/language impaired and control children: speech/language stability and outcome</article-title><source>J Am Acad Child Adolesc Psychiatry</source><year>1994</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>1322</fpage><lpage>1330</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7995800</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><collab>Commission on Classification and Terminology of the International League against Epilepsy</collab><article-title>Proposal for revised classification of epilepsies and epileptic syndromes</article-title><source>Epilepsia</source><year>1989</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>389</fpage><lpage>399</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2502382</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Farrell</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>William</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Tatum</surname><given-names>IV</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Wyllie</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Gupta</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lachhwani</surname><given-names>DK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Encephalopathic Generalized Epilepsy and Lennox-Gastaut Syndrome</article-title><source>